From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerry Zhao <jerryz123@berkeley.edu>
Subject: [PATCH] Bound bubble-sort input for functional simulation
Purpose: Retains bubble-sort behavior with a smaller deterministic CI input.
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

The 256-element input makes this quadratic workload dominate the bounded
Bringup-Bench simulation lane. Use 128 elements only for the Rhodium functional
profile while preserving the upstream default and full sortedness check.

diff --git a/bubble-sort/bubble-sort.c b/bubble-sort/bubble-sort.c
--- a/bubble-sort/bubble-sort.c
+++ b/bubble-sort/bubble-sort.c
@@ -1,7 +1,11 @@
 #include "libmin.h"
 
-// supported sizes: 256 (default), 512, 1024, 2048
+// supported sizes: 128 (bounded), 256 (default), 512, 1024, 2048
+#ifdef BRINGUP_BOUNDED
+#define DATASET_SIZE 128
+#else
 #define DATASET_SIZE 256
+#endif
 int data[DATASET_SIZE];
 
 // total swaps executed so far
